gcc/config/i386/winnt.c's own i386_pe_declare_function_type emits
".def NAME; .scl N; .type N; .endef" around every function this target's
cc1 compiles -- called unconditionally whenever write_symbols != SDB_DEBUG
(i386_pe_start_function, this same file) for every ASM_DECLARE_FUNCTION_NAME,
and unconditionally again for every external function reference
(ASM_OUTPUT_EXTERNAL_LIBCALL, config/i386/cygming.h) -- not something a
command-line flag turns off; PE/COFF's own MS-linker-compatibility
convention, present for every function regardless of -g.

This chain's own AS_FOR_TARGET is this chain's own tcc (9518ca7 --
neither a real `as` nor tcc's linker can bridge the ELF/COFF split this
package's own default.nix documents, so this chain's tcc is what
actually assembles cc1's output). tcc's assembler (tccasm.c/i386-asm.c)
has no .def/.scl/.type/.endef handling at all -- these are a GNU-as
PE-COFF-specific extension for the symbol table a real Microsoft-
compatible linker consults, not part of any assembler tcc was ever
asked to be. Confirmed directly: this package's own functional test
(a plain C program, hello.c, with no -g at all) fails to assemble with
tcc's real error "unknown opcode '.def'" the moment cc1 emits its first
function -- not a guess, the real, minimal failure.

Neutralizing i386_pe_declare_function_type itself (rather than gating
each of its three call sites separately) means every caller stays
correct, real GCC source -- this is the one place PE-symbol-table
markers actually get written to the assembler output, and this target
has no consumer for them: nothing downstream of this bootstrap's own
tcc-assembled, tcc-linked output is a Microsoft linker or anything else
that reads a COFF symbol table's DT_FCN marking. Losing it costs
nothing this chain's own as+ld (also tcc, see default.nix) or any
target program built by this chain's own gcc will ever need.

--- gcc/config/i386/winnt.c
+++ gcc/config/i386/winnt.c
@@ -564,13 +564,14 @@
    visible.  */
 
 void
-i386_pe_declare_function_type (FILE *file, const char *name, int pub)
+i386_pe_declare_function_type (FILE *file ATTRIBUTE_UNUSED,
+				const char *name ATTRIBUTE_UNUSED,
+				int pub ATTRIBUTE_UNUSED)
 {
-  fprintf (file, "\t.def\t");
-  assemble_name (file, name);
-  fprintf (file, ";\t.scl\t%d;\t.type\t%d;\t.endef\n",
-	   pub ? (int) C_EXT : (int) C_STAT,
-	   (int) DT_FCN << N_BTSHFT);
+  /* nova-nix Windows bootstrap: this target's own assembler (this
+     chain's tcc, not a real GNU as) has no .def/.scl/.type/.endef
+     handling -- see def-scl-type.patch's own header for why emitting
+     nothing here is correct, not a loss, for this target. */
 }
 
 /* Keep a list of external functions.  */
